# The generated projection is a function of the tree, never a hand-merged
# surface. It no longer carries a count that every regeneration rewrites, so two
# concurrent regenerations merge as plain text; what can still collide is a row
# inserted at the same position in the same sorted table, which is what this
# driver answers. It is a net, not a requirement: an unarmed clone merges the
# projection by itself, and the local gate's `docs-generated-projection` step
# refuses a projection that no longer matches its sources.
#
# Arm the driver once per checkout (optional): bun scripts/docs-generated-merge.mjs --install
docs/generated/** merge=docs-generated

# Shared-document classes (issue #498): the collision-safe merge layer over the
# documents several concurrent sessions and PRs write. Arm once per checkout
# (optional, same per-checkout git limitation): bun scripts/shared-doc-merge.mjs --install
# An unarmed clone degrades to git's textual merge — verified behavior — and
# the armed drivers add the semantic layer (row union by key; a same-row status
# flip or a differing ceiling leaf surfaces as a real conflict; frozen facts in
# REPOSITORY_STATE.md never union).
docs/ROADMAP.md merge=agentic-shared-roadmap
docs/workflow/SKILL_CONTEXT_BUDGETS.json merge=agentic-shared-budgets
docs/workflow/REPOSITORY_STATE.md merge=agentic-shared-repo-state
